1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,295
Welcome back!

2
00:00:01,295 --> 00:00:04,351
If you spend money on ads,
this lesson is for you.

3
00:00:04,351 --> 00:00:08,569
We'll connect your ad accounts, read
the Google and Facebook reports,

4
00:00:08,569 --> 00:00:13,582
and then use attribution to see which
sources actually turn into paying customers.

5
00:00:14,433 --> 00:00:17,631
Everything lives under
Reporting, in the sidebar.

6
00:00:17,631 --> 00:00:20,763
These advanced reports
are part of the Pro plan.

7
00:00:20,763 --> 00:00:26,114
Across the top, you'll find tabs for Google
Ads, Facebook Ads, attribution, calls,

8
00:00:26,114 --> 00:00:27,876
appointments and your team.

9
00:00:28,734 --> 00:00:31,449
The first time, you'll
see a connect button.

10
00:00:31,449 --> 00:00:35,212
Click it, sign in with the Google
account that runs your ads,

11
00:00:35,212 --> 00:00:37,926
and choose the ad account
for this business.

12
00:00:37,926 --> 00:00:38,543
Then save.

13
00:00:38,543 --> 00:00:41,011
New data can take up to a day to appear.

14
00:00:41,862 --> 00:00:43,531
Here's the last 30 days.

15
00:00:43,531 --> 00:00:46,660
Impressions is how often
your ads were shown.

16
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:49,025
Clicks is how many people visited.

17
00:00:49,025 --> 00:00:52,711
Click-through rate, or CTR,
is the share who clicked,

18
00:00:52,711 --> 00:00:55,771
and average CPC is what
each click cost you.

19
00:00:56,622 --> 00:00:59,014
The second row is about money.

20
00:00:59,014 --> 00:01:03,799
This month, Google cost £844.56,
and brought 11 conversions.

21
00:01:03,799 --> 00:01:06,191
That’s about £77 for each one.

22
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:11,215
Cost per conversion is the number
to compare between campaigns.

23
00:01:12,065 --> 00:01:13,944
Scroll down for each campaign.

24
00:01:13,944 --> 00:01:19,018
Invisalign brings the most conversions,
while the brand campaign is the cheapest,

25
00:01:19,018 --> 00:01:21,398
because those people already know you.

26
00:01:21,398 --> 00:01:25,094
Switch to Keywords to see
exactly what people searched for.

27
00:01:25,943 --> 00:01:32,250
Facebook Ads works the same way, once
you've connected your Facebook page and ad

28
00:01:32,250 --> 00:01:32,881
account.

29
00:01:32,881 --> 00:01:36,034
Here we spent £612.40, and got 14 leads.

30
00:01:36,034 --> 00:01:38,872
That's a cost per lead of about £44.

31
00:01:39,724 --> 00:01:42,732
The donut shows where
those leads came from.

32
00:01:42,732 --> 00:01:46,492
The Invisalign free scan
campaign brought 10 of the 14.

33
00:01:46,492 --> 00:01:51,552
Below, you can drill down from campaigns,
into ad sets and individual ads,

34
00:01:51,552 --> 00:01:54,013
to find the creative that’s working.

35
00:01:54,862 --> 00:01:58,105
Clicks and leads are only half the story.

36
00:01:58,105 --> 00:02:03,168
The Attribution Report follows
each lead all the way to revenue.

37
00:02:03,168 --> 00:02:08,864
In the last 30 days, 46 leads came
in, 4 became won deals, worth £7,100.

38
00:02:09,713 --> 00:02:11,237
Each row is a source.

39
00:02:11,237 --> 00:02:15,009
Paid Social brought 14
leads, and £3,800 of revenue.

40
00:02:15,009 --> 00:02:18,129
Click a row to see the
campaigns inside it,

41
00:02:18,129 --> 00:02:21,539
so you know exactly which
ad earned that money.

42
00:02:22,391 --> 00:02:25,633
At the top, switch between
first and last attribution.

43
00:02:25,633 --> 00:02:29,056
First gives credit to the
source that brought someone in.

44
00:02:29,056 --> 00:02:32,118
Last credits the final
touch before they converted.

45
00:02:32,118 --> 00:02:36,922
Looking at both tells you which channels
find people, and which ones close them.

46
00:02:37,778 --> 00:02:39,169
So how do you use this?

47
00:02:39,169 --> 00:02:43,888
Compare cost per lead between channels,
but judge them on revenue, not clicks.

48
00:02:43,888 --> 00:02:48,304
And give each campaign at least a
month of data before you switch it off.

49
00:02:48,304 --> 00:02:51,631
A single good patient can
pay for a whole month of ads.

50
00:02:52,482 --> 00:02:53,707
Here’s a pro tip.

51
00:02:53,707 --> 00:02:58,752
Add UTM parameters to every link in
your ads, emails and social posts,

52
00:02:58,752 --> 00:03:00,553
like utm_source=facebook.

53
00:03:00,553 --> 00:03:03,940
Kyntlo reads them when
someone fills in a form,

54
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:08,048
so your attribution report
can tell every campaign apart.

55
00:03:08,898 --> 00:03:11,282
Now you know what your
ads really bring in.

56
00:03:11,282 --> 00:03:15,051
Next, we'll look at calls, appointments
and your team's performance.

57
00:03:15,051 --> 00:03:15,827
See you there!
